  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project formulation Africa Regional Integration and Trade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the consultancy assignment is to provide technical support to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs/Learning in identifying and developing two projects which will support actions for increased trade and regional economic integration in Africa; the consultancy will assist in preparing the necessary project documentation for the suggested interventions in line with the Danida Aid Management Guidelines. 

The working hypothesis is that the support will be provided to East African Community (EAC) and Economic Committeion of West African States (ECOWAS) to strengthen their capacities and efforts to perform their roles in promoting inclusive and sustainable trade and economic integration in the East and West African regions respectively. 
To support MFA in drafting the Project Documents(PD) the consultants will:  
1.	Follow the AMG in describing the context and justification for the usage of funds allocated, outline key principles and financing modalities; theory of change and results framework, budgets and how the instrument interacts with and complements other financial support from member states and donors. The aim is to support the chosen competent authorities in addressing urgent political priorities over the next 2-3 years without distorting or complicating the existing structures and procedures.

2.	Prepare a project document for each envisaged engagement. Each document  will include all relevant supporting documentation ready for submission to and final approval by the Minister for Foreign Affairs. The programming process and project development, and documentation  shall follow the guidelines published in the Danida Aid Management Guidelines for projects between DKK 10 &#x2013; 43 million.</narrative>
  </description>
